From b1916edd16a3dc560e0de33f4bbdb52265b74043 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Parsonage <eric@eparsonage.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:20:36 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Count each CRLF as two characters in Racket positions

With line counting on, Racket reads "\r\n" as one position, while the
editor counts two characters, so every syntax, srcloc and lexer position
in a CRLF document was one character early for each CRLF before it.
Expansion, the lexer and the formatter's lexer now read the document
through a port that keeps Racket's lines and columns but reports
positions in characters.
